+## New discriminator — supremeai-core main advanced past the referenced red commit
+
+The #2225 finding named CI run 40653481018 (failure, head feda45e4,
+2026-10-28T07:58Z) as the prime root-cause candidate via autoDeploy correlation.
+#2901 (22:41Z) found main frozen at feda45e4d across 24h of samples. This probe
+finds main has since unfrozen and advanced through at least five distinct heads on
+2026-10-29 (main-branch run `head_sha` observations, schedule plane):
+
+| observed at (run created_at) | main head |
+|---|---|
+| 09:13:32Z | 6e85767b |
+| 10:05:10Z | e23088a8 |
+| 16:56:58Z | 7b081ef0 |
+| 21:25:23Z | 27dd3b83 |
+| 21:50:06Z | f659b653 |
+
+Yet both services still report `update_failed` at 23:14Z. Implication
+(hypothesis-weakening, not conclusion): if autoDeploy were healthy, any of these
+heads should have produced a live deploy; a residual that survives five-plus fresh
+heads is no longer well explained by one bad commit (feda45e4). The failure is
+persistent across fresh main heads, which strengthens the case that the next
+diagnostic must be Render-side build logs per service (admin-only), not further
+core-CI archaeology. Equally possible: autoDeploy triggers are not firing at all
+(deploys never attempted) — the two hypotheses are indistinguishable from the
+zero-credential plane, which is precisely why the admin lane owns the next step.
+
+Tool-window caveat: `github.workflow_runs` (perPage=30) returned a 5-row window on
